  "request": "#963 slice 7 (r8, r9, r10):\nr8 · A status never moves backward within a step: `--step plan --status planned` then `--step plan --status planning` currently regresses it, because the guard compares steps only (`spec_context.py` around line 397) and status is set unconditionally (`write-context.py` around line 224)\nr9 · A damaged `.spec-context.json` is kept aside, never silently replaced: today a truncated or unparseable record reads as empty and the next write starts fresh history (`spec_context.py` `read_ctx`, around lines 686-701 and 732). Quarantine it the way a non-list `history` already is, and say so in the run's output\nr10 · Property tests for the record writer's promises (history only grows, writes merge, status never backward, parallel writers lose nothing, damaged records kept): Hypothesis, about a minute, marked slow. Start from `speckit-sandboxes/evidence/2026-11-07-pdd-lite/properties_test.py`\nAcceptance: A same-step status write that would move backward is refused, and a damaged record is kept aside with a message. The property tests run in the suite (slow lane) and pass.",
